body:
`MetadataWatchCallback` introduces a third event-shape/naming scheme (`registered|updated|unregistered`) that doesn't match `MetadataEventSchema.event` (`metadata.registered`, etc.) in the new protocol. This divergence will make it harder for implementations/consumers to share event handling. Consider reusing `MetadataEvent` (or at least aligning naming/fields) for the watch callback payload.
```suggestion
import type { MetadataQuery, MetadataQueryResult, MetadataValidationResult, MetadataBulkResult, MetadataDependency, MetadataEvent } from '../kernel/metadata-plugin.zod';
import type { MetadataOverlay } from '../kernel/metadata-customization.zod';

/**
 * Metadata watch callback signature
 *
 * Uses the canonical MetadataEvent protocol shape to ensure
 * consistent event naming (e.g. `metadata.registered`) and fields.
 */
export type MetadataWatchCallback = (event: MetadataEvent) => void;
```
